###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Schema 0.1.2 has no run-level optimiser property (v0.2.0 proposal in METHODS.md), so the optimiser and the training targets are paper-local string settings. Standard deviations over the five seeds (Table 1) are not encoded; one run per configuration stands for the five seeds.
# - The data sets are reused from the cited Allegro (CDP) and NequIP (water) studies; sizes, splits and reference levels are not restated in the text read, so the data-set nodes carry no reference calculation. For the Allegro model, 'number of scalar features' (32, with 32 tensor features) is encoded as numFeatures; numEpochs is the maximum.
# - Runs with 5%, 10%, 50% and 75% force labels (Figure 1, Table 5), optimiser hyperparameters (Table 4), wall-clock comparisons and MD observables are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
